},{"id":"01-WR","theme":1,"themeTitle":"The Family","sourcePage":1,"strand":"Writing","title":"The Family: Functional Writing — Completing Forms","focus":"Functional Writing — Completing Forms","lessons":2,"outcomes":["Identify the audience and the expected features of functional writing: completing forms for a message about family roles, kind choices and everyday routines.","Plan and write a home contact form with a clear purpose, logical organisation and appropriate vocabulary.","Edit the draft for legibility, punctuation and spelling, then explain one meaningful improvement."],"inquiry":["What does a reader need to understand from a home contact form?","How does revising our writing make it easier to read?"],"experiences":["Study a short teacher-written model of a home contact form and discuss what makes it useful.","Draft an original response, peer-check purpose and conventions, and improve the final copy."],"resources":"Original writing model, planning frame, notebooks and self-editing checklist.","assessment":"Completed writing product with purpose, organisation, language accuracy and evidence of revision.","competencies":"Communication and collaboration; critical thinking; creativity; self-efficacy; digital literacy where safe and available."},{"id":"02-LS","theme":2,"themeTitle":"Family Celebrations","sourcePage":8,"strand":"Listening and Speaking","title":"Family Celebrations: Pronunciation and Vocabulary — Target Sounds","focus":"Pronunciation and Vocabulary — Target Sounds","lessons":2,"outcomes":["Listen attentively to a birthday invitation and replies and report two accurate details using the topic vocabulary.","Practise pronunciation and vocabulary: target sounds in a short paired exchange, checking pronunciation, clarity and respectful turn-taking.","Respond orally to a follow-up question about planning a family celebration and thanking guests using an appropriate tone and complete thought."],"inquiry":["How does careful listening improve a conversati